<!--Post: 7738--><!--Time: 1108670530-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7738"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://sunflower.wichita.edu/2004/08/25/btk.asp" target=_top>http://sunflower.wichita.edu/2004/08/25/btk.asp</a> <BR>Wyatt taught American folklore &#40;English 440 from 1964 to spring 1973, English 540 from fall 1973 to 1977, currently English 342&#41; at 8:30 or 10:30 a.m. Mondays, Wednesdays and Fridays in Jardine Hall, according to course catalogs in the Special Collections department of the WSU library. <BR> <BR>Wyatt&#39;s initials, P.J., appear in a list of what appear to be book chapters under the heading &#34;The BTK Story,&#34; part of a letter sent to KAKE last May. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7738-->
<!--Post: 7739--><!--Time: 1108670891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7739"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Amandab<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Amandab<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And where is P.J. Wyatt now?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7739-->
<!--Post: 7742--><!--Time: 1108671224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7742"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jackal<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jackal<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->She died of &#34;natural&#34; causes some 10 to 12 yrs ago.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7742-->
<!--Post: 7743--><!--Time: 1108671230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7743"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->She is no longer with us..she died.   <BR> <BR>I personally think Pj&#39;s refers to something else..perhaps pajamas/lingerie?  I&#39;m not sure, but I don&#39;t think she was THAT important to him.  I could be wrong, though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7743-->
<!--Post: 7744--><!--Time: 1108671709-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7744"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If PJ taught classes on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays, then BTK could&#39;ve gone to those classes &#40;possibly&#41; or watched them and that would leave Tuesdays and Thursdays open for BTK to kill then, right?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7744-->
<!--Post: 7745--><!--Time: 1108671862-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7745"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->anyone knows what PJ &#40;Wyatt&#41; stands for?  <BR> <BR>what her first/middle name was? I have researched it but it is NOWHERE to be found. <BR> <BR>I think the chapter PJ stands for  <BR>&#34;Photo Journal&#34; his collection of photos of his dead victims, maybe also pictures he took while stalking them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7745-->
<!--Post: 7748--><!--Time: 1108672140-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7748"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, I just read her first name was Phoebe over at AMW.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m more inclined to believe the Photo Journal as opposed to her.  That is something that would be far more important to him than a passing English/folklore teacher, IMHO.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7748-->
<!--Post: 7764--><!--Time: 1108675430-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7764"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 1:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It was Pheobe J. Wyatt, can&#39;t find anything about what the J. stands for.   <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/9463452.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/archive/9463452.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Just as an FYI<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7764-->
<!--Post: 7781--><!--Time: 1108682399-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7781"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 3:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Under this General BTK Discussion topic page go to the Oh Death and PJ thread and scroll down to near the bottom, there I have posted PJ Wyatt&#39;s class schedules.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7781-->
<!--Post: 7786--><!--Time: 1108683356-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7786"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov..I agree that the PJ mentioned as a title to a chapter refers to PHOTO JOURNALS.  I guess it depends on how it is written...If it is written as P.J. then I would think BTK is referring to a person whose initials are P.J. since there is a sifnificant person in this case who has the initials P.J. <BR>PJ&#39;s are usually not initialed with dots after both letters.   <BR>PJ could mean either P.J. Wyatt or Photo Journal...but I think P.J. Wyatt would have been referenced with P . J . <BR> <BR>I just wonder why they called her P.J....I know that initials usually are given to MEN as nick names or shorts...but I guess a woman can have them too. Thanks..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7786-->
<!--Post: 7788--><!--Time: 1108683463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 3:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know whether or not P.J. Wyatt ever had any children?  Thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7788-->
<!--Post: 7815--><!--Time: 1108689529-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7815"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 5:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Featherw <BR> <BR>Here is all I could find about P J Wyatt having any children. It seems like she had one child but I can´t tell from the wordings if that child is dead or alive? <BR> <BR>It is actually strange that it is almost impossible to find any info on P J Wyatt. Her first name Phoebe is only to be found ONE place on the net, and there is NOTHING about her child, nothing about her death, no obituaries nada nada hmmm wonder why? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/9463452.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/archive/9463452.htm</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>There was no funeral for P.J. Wyatt when she died 13 years ago in Wichita. An only child who never married, she had no surviving family. <BR> <BR>Her obituary simply asked for donations to Hospice Inc. and the Wichita Center for the Arts. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7815-->
<!--Post: 7818--><!--Time: 1108691961-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7818"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 5:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->SKOV...thanks.  I find it interesting that there was no funeral for her..NO FUNERAL after all she seemed to do for society.  She was a teacher...and seemed to be admired by some.  She even operated the radio supply company owned by her father D.F. Wyatt by herself in the 70&#39;s.  Surely she should have had a funeral.  <BR>Thanks for brininging that out! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7818-->
<!--Post: 7823--><!--Time: 1108693061-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Her father was longtime Wichita buisnessman David F. Wyatt &#40;1897-1972&#41;. <BR>She died in 1991 and suggested donations be made to Hospice Inc. and the Wichita Center of the Arts. <BR>She was an only child and never married. <BR>Her closest friend and former housemate was the former WSU English professor Anita Skeen.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7823-->
<!--Post: 7824--><!--Time: 1108693360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7824"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Her closest friend and former housemate was the former WSU English professor Anita Skeen.  <BR>  <BR>That&#39;s just a nice way of saying she was gay, IMHO.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7824-->
<!--Post: 7826--><!--Time: 1108694457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7826"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jilleng<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jilleng<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I searched the social security death index and found P.J. Wyatt&#39;s social security number..i know there are programs out there that if you plug in her social security number, besides her personal info, all her known associates and relatives will pop up for her also...we have the program at work but i don&#39;t dare run it...so for those that have access to a search program like that and want to run her social # to see associates...her number is 511-24-2220...it&#39;s public knowledge and posted on the ssdi website so no one should get into any trouble for running it..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7826-->
<!--Post: 7827--><!--Time: 1108698289-->
