<!--/Post: 7827-->
<!--Post: 7923--><!--Time: 1108748164-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7923"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 9:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, her name wasn&#39;t &#34;Phoebe&#34; it was Phyllis. No wonder she went by PJ!  <BR> <BR>Phyllis Wyatt -- better known by the nickname P.J. She died in 1991. <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/9509651.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/9509651.htm</a> <BR> <BR>I found her family listed in the 1930 Cencus living at Minneola, Clark Co., Ks.  Her father David F., born in Missouri; her mother Stella, born in Ks. and Phyllis &#40;age 3 7/12&#41;, born in Ks.  <BR>Her father was an auto salesman at that time. <BR> <BR>Father David died Feb. 1972 in Wichita, Ks. <BR>Mother Stella died Oct. 1977 in Wichita, Ks. <BR> <BR>Still looking for more info. If I find anything, I will post. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7923-->
<!--Post: 7926--><!--Time: 1108749701-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 10:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The Heroines&#34;  P.J. Wyatt honored by friend Anita Skeen: <BR><a href="http://plaza.twsu.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay.asp?ID=868" target=_top>http://plaza.twsu.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay. asp?ID=868</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7926-->
<!--Post: 7963--><!--Time: 1108768088-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7963"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tadpole...you are wonderful.  Thank YOu.  I noticed in the profile of BTK that he had a cousin named SUSAN who lived in Missouri was it?  I will have to recheck the exact name of the cousin in Missouri...but I believe that is it.  AMAZING.  For all we know, Missouri may be a key place in this ...given that her father was born there.   <BR> <BR>I bet BTK has family in Missouri...just a guess.  <BR>Thanks..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7963-->
<!--Post: 7975--><!--Time: 1108771262-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7975"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tadpole...thank you very much! you have been a grat help! <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7975-->
<!--Post: 7980--><!--Time: 1108772272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7980"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re welcome &#40;blushing&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Petra Tasheff brick info. <a href="http://plaza.twsu.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay.asp?ID=755" target=_top>http://plaza.twsu.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay. asp?ID=755</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;Petra &#34;Tedde&#34; Tasheff, who was student body president in 1976-77...&#34;  <BR><a href="http://www.kuconnection.org/feb2002/people_DavidAmbler.asp" target=_top>http://www.kuconnection.org/feb2002/people_DavidAm bler.asp</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;Dec. 2, 2004 -- the Tasheff family issued a statement saying that Petra Tasheff, known as &#34;Tedde,&#34; in their family is not the same Petra mentioned by the BTK. The Tasheff family is of Bulgarian descent, not Hispanic, and has never lived near a railroad; and their Petra Tasheff has no younger sister.&#34; <BR><a href="http://johnsville.blogspot.com/2004/04/btk-bind-torture-kill-strangler-info.html" target=_top>http://johnsville.blogspot.com/2004/04/btk-bind-to rture-kill-strangler-info.html</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7980-->
<!--Post: 7982--><!--Time: 1108772454-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7982"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oops, that really doesn&#39;t belong here, but I found it interesting and ties her into the college years in 1970&#39;s.   <BR> <BR>By doing a search on her, she is quite accomplished. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7982-->
<!--Post: 7983--><!--Time: 1108773036-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7983"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh, Oh!  But Petra did have a younger sister Christine!  Found this obit published in  <BR>&#34;The Leader Herald&#34; Gloversville, NY, Thurs. Jan. 20, 2005:  But, please respect their privacy. This obit is a matter of public record due to it being on the internet.  <BR> <BR>James Anton Tasheff  <BR> <BR>Mrs. Magdaline Folmsbee and Mrs. Virginia Baker have received word of the death of their brother, James Anton Tasheff, age 80, on November 11, 2004.  <BR> <BR> <BR>Mr. Tasheff was the son of Petra and Stoil Tasheff of Gloversville. He attended Gloversville Schools and Columbia University before entering the Army and serving as a combat Infantryman in Europe during World War II. He married Mary Louise Southworth of Wichita, Kansas on July 14, 1945. They settled in Wichita, Kansas, where he founded the T &amp; M Oil Company and later Kansas Petroleum Inc. in which he was still active at the time of his death. Jim was a respected force in the Kansas oil industry.  <BR> <BR>Mr. Tasheff was survived by is wife of 59 years and a son, Steven Tasheff of San Francisco; a daughter, Marni Vliet of Wichita; a daughter, Petra Tasheff of New York City and a daughter, Christine Tasheff of Wichita. His sister, Mary Tasheff of Canada Lake passed away on the same date.  <BR>Mr. Tasheff was a member of the Grace Presbyterian Church in Wichita, Kansas, where a memorial service was held on November 14, 2004.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://216.109.117.135/search/cache?p=Petra%2BTasheff&amp;toggle=1&amp;ei=UTF-8&amp;xargs=0&amp;pstart=1&amp;b=11&amp;u=www.leaderherald.com/obit/story/0120202005_obtTasheffobit0120.asp&amp;w=petra%2Btasheff&amp;d=77E1774939&amp;icp=1&amp;.intl=us" target=_top>http://216.109.117.135/search/cache?p=Petra&#43;Tashef f&amp;toggle=1&amp;ei=UTF-8&amp;xargs=0&amp;pstart=1&amp;b=11&amp;u=www.le aderherald.com/obit/story/0120202005_obtTasheffobi t0120.asp&amp;w=petra&#43;tasheff&amp;d=77E1774939&amp;icp=1&amp;.intl =us</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7983-->
<!--Post: 7999--><!--Time: 1108781220-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://weberstudies.weber.edu/archive/archive%20A%20%20Vol.%201-10.3/Vol.%207.1/7.1skeen.htm" target=_top>http://weberstudies.weber.edu/archive/archive%20A% 20%20Vol.%201-10.3/Vol.%207.1/7.1skeen.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Anita SKEEN poetry...another page... <BR> <BR>Humanities Seminar <BR> <BR>Excerpted from the page: <BR>        4. <BR> <BR>A woman drives south down the interstate <BR>to see her lover. <BR>She suspects this is the last <BR>time. She concentrates hard. <BR>She turns all their names over  <BR>again and again <BR>like unfamiliar rocks. <BR>She procounces them sofly, <BR>sifts the vowels from the consonants. <BR>........<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7999-->
<!--Post: 8005--><!--Time: 1108785997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8005"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 8:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if this is Ms. Wyatt&#39;s work: <BR>207.44.240.63/~lyricsp/alpha/songs/i/iwantyoubacka gain.shtml  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8005-->
<!--Post: 8006--><!--Time: 1108786212-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8006"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 8:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Shucks, that link didn&#39;t work :-&#40;  Here are the words: <BR> <BR>I WANT YOU BACK AGAIN <BR>&#40;Phyllis Wyatt / W.M. Johnson&#41; <BR> <BR>Carl Perkins <BR> <BR> <BR>No-one had to tell me twice <BR>When the fire went out <BR>I didn&amp;#65533;t know what true love meant <BR>But now I have no doubt <BR> <BR>For looking back it had to be <BR>I see what I have lost <BR>I don&amp;#65533;t know how I lost you <BR>But I want you back again <BR> <BR>Lord I miss you touching me <BR>And taking all my time <BR>And since you don&amp;#65533;t love me <BR>I miss you being mine <BR> <BR>Haven&amp;#65533;t you been losing ???? <BR>????  my craziest ???? <BR>I only know I love you <BR>And I want you back again <BR> <BR>Have I burnt the candle <BR>For so long that it&amp;#65533;s gone <BR>It&amp;#65533;s too ???? <BR>But now ???? <BR> <BR>I never meant to hurt you <BR>Understand if you can <BR>Lord it hurts to lose you <BR>And I want you back again <BR> <BR>Have I burnt the candle <BR>For so long that it&amp;#65533;s gone <BR>It&amp;#65533;s too ????? <BR>But now ????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8006-->
<!--Post: 8009--><!--Time: 1108786617-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8009"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 8:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoa!  I don&#39;t know where that &#34;it&amp;#65533;s&#34; came from, but that isn&#39;t on the web site!  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8009-->
<!--Post: 8011--><!--Time: 1108786957-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8011"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 8:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let me guess it is one of those that does not come up until you copy and paste it somewhere?  Yep...I have run in to those before...strange.. <BR>Thanks for posting this. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8011-->
<!--Post: 8042--><!--Time: 1108831799-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8042"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 8:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->More about Anita Skeen: <BR><a href="http://www.lib.msu.edu/vincent/writers/fall99/091099.htm" target=_top>www.lib.msu.edu/vincent/writers/fall99/091099.htm</a>  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.msupress.msu.edu/bookTemplate.php?bookID=480" target=_top>http://www.msupress.msu.edu/bookTemplate.php?bookI D=480</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.junebugbookstore.com/si/12012.html" target=_top>www.junebugbookstore.com/si/12012.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8042-->
<!--Post: 8160--><!--Time: 1108933058-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8160"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 12:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I WANT YOU BACK AGAIN  <BR>&#40;Phyllis Wyatt / W.M. Johnson&#41;  <BR> <BR>Carl Perkins  <BR> <BR> <BR>Carl Perkins is a Rockabilly musician.  A very good one I might add.  Very close to the folk style...just a little FASTER with more drums. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
